 AST receipt puts the call at 2906.\nREQUIRED_RECHECK: (1) The construction site of `candles`/`latest` feeding run-empire-v2.js:1748 and 2906 — show the code that builds those candle objects and the unit of `.t`/`.etime` (is it broker REST ms, or `storeTimeframeCandle` output in seconds?). (2) An AST scan extended to all tracked root-level JS files and `tools/` confirming no additional `updateLastPrice` references.\nRECHECK_PROMPT: \"Mercury: supply host-attested excerpts showing where the `candles` array consumed at run-empire-v2.js:1731 (REST hydration) and run-empire-v2.js:2890 (liveness recovery) is populated, including the exact assignment of the `.t` and `.etime` fields, and state whether those values are epoch milliseconds or seconds at that point. If they can ever be seconds (e.g., sourced from candles stored via storeTimeframeCandle after normalizeOhlcForProcessor), state whether the new ms-normalized SessionRouter mark permanently blocks those callers via the monotonic gate at core/StateManager.js:906. Also rerun the Acorn updateLastPrice reference scan extended to all tracked root-level *.js files and tools/, and report the full ref list.\"\nNEXT_CHECK: `grep -n \"etime\" run-empire-v2.js` around the hydration candle-build sites plus inspection of `storeTimeframeCandle`'s stored timestamp unit, on the trusted host.\nCANDIDATE SET: examined 9 of 9 supplied attested artifacts (M ≥ 3 touched files: run-empire-v2.js, test/aggregate-source-backfill.test.js, CHANGELOG.md — all 3 examined). Candidates: run-empire-v2.js:465-532; run-empire-v2.js:885-995; run-empire-v2.js:1731-1750; run-empire-v2.js:2890-2908; core/StateManager.js:892-920; foundation/ohlc-normalize.js:35-62; test/aggregate-source-backfill.test.js:21-78; CHANGELOG.md:8-15; EVIDENCE.md:1-170 (incl. AST receipt with 7 refs, probe output, 4 prior run ledger entries). Unexamined candidates named in DID NOT EXAMINE.\nAST EVIDENCE: I have no repo tools in this pass; the only AST evidence is the host-carried Acorn receipt in EVIDENCE.md (155/155 files, 0 parse failures, 7 refs, no computed/aliased/destructured calls). Its line numbers are consistent with the excerpts. Named absence: scan universe excludes root-level JS other than run-empire-v2.js, `test/`, `tools/`, `public/js/` — and root runtime files demonstrably exist.\nINHERITED: run-empire-v2.js — `latest.etime || latest.t` falsy-zero fallback at 1748 and 2906 (unfixed); `|| 'unknown'` / `|| null` silent defaults in trace payloads (895-903, 897); `(this.timeframeSelector && this.timeframeSelector.currentTimeframe) || this.candleTimeframe` silent active-tf fallback (unfixed). core/StateManager.js (cited, untouched) — `eventTimeMs = Date.now()` silent default parameter; `getLastPrice` returns `|| null` (a legitimate 0-price collapse is unreachable given the >0 write gate, but the pattern is inherited, unfixed). test file — textual assertions only, no swallowed catches. CHANGELOG.md — n/a.\nFOURTH SHAPE CLASSIFIER: classified 3 of 3 added constructs. (1) `markEventTimeMs = ohlcTimestampMs(ohlcData[1])` — producer-fixable and it IS the authorized producer fix. (2) `canUpdateLastPrice` guard + `mark_unavailable` ternary arm — true boundary (writer availability at a component seam; pre-existing existence check made explicit and traced). (3) `markUpdated ? 'mark_updated' : 'mark_rejected'` — true boundary reporting of the pre-existing StateManager monotonic gate; no new gate added. Unchanged StateManager rejection is out of diff and correctly untouched per the ruling.\nALLEGATIONS: A1 SUBSTANTIVE/TESTIMONY — millisecond-unit claim for callers at 1748/2906 is prose-only; wrong-direction risk if seconds. A2 MECHANICAL/RECEIPT — AST totality universe excludes root-level runtime JS proven to exist by the TierFeatureFlags require. A3 MECHANICAL/TESTIMONY — the \"trusted host probe\" output and jest/`node --check` results are carried inside an attested document; the manifest attests file bytes, not command execution, so their execution provenance is document-carried, not a host-attested trusted-path test receipt. A4 MECHANICAL/RECEIPT — tests are predominantly `indexOf`/`toContain` source scans; no behavioral test drives the actual handler with a synthetic event to prove end-to-end conversion. A5 MECHANICAL/RECEIPT — `mark_rejected` also fires for invalid-price false returns from `updateLastPrice`, slightly overloading \"rejected\" beyond staleness (label remains defensible). A6 MECHANICAL/RECEIPT — EVIDENCE cites caller range 2842-2905 while its own AST receipt places the call at 2906. TESTIMONY-based A1 cannot raise found_break; it caps at needs_more_evidence.\nSUBSTANTIVE RESOLUTION: none — A1 is an evidence gap awaiting the recheck, not a non-convergence between seats; Mercury seat was absent (HTTP 402) and Kimi seat absent, so no multi-seat position exists to quote.\nWHAT I EXAMINED: all nine host-attested excerpts and the manifest hashes; the Acorn reference receipt JSON; the probe command and its JSON output; the four prior adversarial run summaries; internal line-number consistency between the AST receipt and the three caller excerpts; the trace-emission ordering versus the `if (tf === activeTf)` branch; the test file's assertions against the handler excerpt.\nDID NOT EXAMINE: construction of `candles`/`latest` at the REST hydration and liveness sites; `storeTimeframeCandle` / `storeSymbolTimeframeCandle` stored timestamp units; `normalizeOhlc` itself (only its consumer); `emitTrace` implementation; SessionRouter `_transitionToCrypto` consumer of `getLastPrice`; root-level JS files other than run-empire-v2.js; `tools/`, `public/js/`, `test/` beyond the supplied excerpt; the actual git diff against predecessor 4878c01; live runtime behavior.\nASSUMED: the manifest hashes genuinely bind excerpts to HEAD artifacts; the pre-change handler line quoted in EVIDENCE.md matches the predecessor commit; the Acorn receipt was produced by the host as described; `normalizeOhlc` output inde